New browser UI (server/web, stage 4):

- Beautiful UI (https://www.beautifului.dev, MIT): Thinking (native reasoning
  disclosure/activity), Streaming Text (stream cursor/fade), Tool Chips (command
  disclosure), Approval Card (dialogs), Task Rows (table/queue/inventory), Code
  Block, Diff Table, Prompt Bar (composer/attachments), and Chat (transcript,
  sidebar and theme tokens). Adaptations are in src/main.ts, src/elements.ts and
  src/app.css. The frozen client's MIT Beautiful UI adaptations were consulted
  for Thinking and Prompt Bar, and its Beautiful UI theme tokens were adapted.
  No frozen protocol code was restored. The stage-4 polish additionally adapts
  Tool Chips' compact title/status/metrics row and completed disclosure, Prompt
  Bar's inset growing editor, round attach/send/stop controls and compact
  pickers, and Chat's spacing, empty state, segmented session filters and tabs.
  These are plain DOM/CSS implementations, not copied React components.
- Tailwind CSS (https://tailwindcss.com, MIT): standalone CLI v4.3.3 generates
  dist/app.css, including Tailwind's base styles. The CLI is a build tool and
  is not embedded in atto. Its checksum-pinned releases are used by gen.go.
- Vercel AI Elements (https://elements.ai-sdk.dev): design/behavior reference
  only for Queue, Checkpoint, Context, Confirmation, Reasoning/Chain of Thought,
  Tool, Plan/Task, Prompt Input/Model Selector/Attachments, Shimmer, Agent and
  Terminal. No source copied or bundled; no license compatibility assumed.

There is no Preact/React/Radix/Next.js runtime in the new plain TypeScript DOM
bundle. esbuild/goja are existing Go dependencies (MIT), used for build/tests.

